\n\nReason: The knight fork with N: g4-f2 is clearly the best move. It gives check to the White king on e1, forcing White to respond to the check. Since the king must move, I will then capture the rook on h1 on my next turn, winning a full rook (worth about 5 points of material). This is a game-winning advantage that White cannot prevent.\n\nAnswer: N: g4-f2"}
