ical opportunities available.\n\n5. **P: e5-e4** - Advancing the pawn with some space gain, but doesn't address immediate tactical concerns.\n\nReason: **Q: d8-h4** is the strongest move. It accomplishes multiple goals:\n- Attacks the weak g4 pawn\n- Threatens the exposed White king on e1\n- Prevents White from castling comfortably\n- Creates immediate tactical threats\n- The queen on h4 coordinates well with my bishop on c5, creating a dangerous attacking formation\n\nThis move exploits White's main weakness (the uncastled king) while I can still castle on my next move if needed.\n\nAnswer: Q: d8-h4"}
