 down significant material (missing my Queen), I need to create active threats and complications. **B: e1-h4** is the most forcing move, activating my bishop with tempo by threatening White's kingside structure and potentially supporting an attack. The bishop on h4 can coordinate with my other pieces and creates immediate tactical threats. This is more dynamic than passive pawn moves and gets my pieces into the game quickly, which is crucial when behind in material.\n\nAnswer: B: e1-h4"}
