 forcing move compels White to respond immediately, either by moving the King or blocking. Given that White's King is awkwardly placed on e2 with limited escape squares, this check disrupts White's position and maintains my active piece placement. After the King moves, I can continue to exploit its exposed position. This is the most forcing continuation that keeps maximum pressure on White.\n\nAnswer: B: e3-f2"}
