e or win material.\n\nReason: Q: d1-d3+ delivers check and forces White's king to move to a worse square. After the king moves (likely to f4, e2, or f2), I can continue the attack with my queen and bishop working together. This move maintains maximum pressure and doesn't allow White any counterplay. The check is forcing and keeps the initiative firmly in my hands, which is crucial when the opponent's king is this exposed.\n\nAnswer: Q: d1-d3"}
