k to the exposed White king on d3, forcing White to move the king and losing time. After the king moves (likely Kd2, Ke3, or Kc3), my knight will be actively placed on e2, forking potential targets and maintaining pressure. Checks are forcing moves that limit my opponent's options and allow me to dictate the tempo of the game. This tactical blow exploits White's centralized but vulnerable king position.\n\nAnswer: N: d4-e2"}
