g to move to a worse square. This creates immediate tactical pressure and maintains my active knight in a strong position where it can continue to harass White's pieces. Checking moves are often strong as they limit the opponent's options and seize the initiative. After the king moves, I can continue to improve my position with my other pieces.\n\nAnswer: N: d4-c2"}
