 tempo, disrupts White's coordination, and allows me to seize the initiative. In an endgame with material advantage, forcing moves that activate pieces and restrict the opponent's King are crucial. After the King moves, I can bring my Rook into the game more effectively or continue harassing with the Knight.\n\nAnswer: N: e2-c1"}
