 than delivering immediate threats.\n\nReason: **N: e3-g2** delivers check, forcing White's king to move (likely Kg1 is the only legal move). This is the most forcing move available. In winning positions with material advantage, forcing moves that restrict the opponent's options are optimal. After Kg1, I can continue to coordinate my pieces for a mating attack or further restrict the White king while advancing my pawns safely.\n\nAnswer: N: e3-g2"}
