\n1 |RBF1|    |    |    |    |    |    |    | 1\n  +----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----+\n     a    b    c    d    e    f    g    h \nYour valid moves are (src-dst-promotion, or src-dst):\n[R: a1-a2, R: a1-a3, R: a1-a4, R: a1-a5, R: a1-a6, R: a1-a7, R: a1-a8, R: a1-b1, R: a1-c1, R: a1-d1, R: a1-e1, R: a1-f1, R: a1-g1, R: a1-h1, P: b6-b5, P: c7-c5, P: c7-c6, B: c8-b7, B: c8-a6, P: d7-d5, P: d7-d6, K: f7-e6, K: f7-e7, K: f7-e8, K: f7-f8, K: f7-g8]\nYour answer format should be: Answer: piece-name: move. \nPiece-name and move (src-dst-promotion or src-dst) should be directly copied EXACTLY from valid move list.\nExample of valid output format: N: a1-b3; P: e7-e8-q; Piece B: g5-f4.\nPlease select a move from your valid moves that maximize your probability of winning.\n', 'reasoning': '', 'output': "Situation: I'm playing as Black in an endgame position. I have a rook on a1, a bishop on c8, a king on f7, and pawns on b6, c7, d7, and g6. White has a king on f2 and pawns on g5 and h6. Material-wise, I'm significantly ahead with a rook and bishop versus just two pawns. My king is relatively active, and White's pawns are advanced but not immediately threatening.\n\nEvaluation: \n1. **R: a1-a2** - Attacks the white king, forcing it to move. This creates immediate pressure and restricts White's king mobility.\n2. **R: a1-f1** - Cuts off the white king from moving to the first rank, controlling a key file.\n3. **K: f7-e6** - Activates my king toward the center and White's pawns, helping to blockade and eventually capture them.\n4. **P: d7-d5** - Advances a pawn, but doesn't address the immediate position.\n\nThe most forcing move is attacking the white king directly with the rook. R: a1-a2 puts the king in check, limiting White's options and allowing me to dictate the tempo. After the king moves (likely to e3, f3, g3, or similar), I can continue improving my position with my superior material advantage.\n\nReason: Checking the king with R: a1-a2 is the strongest move because:\n- It forces White's response\n- It improves my rook's activity\n- It pushes the white king away from defensive positions\n- With my overwhelming material advantage, active play will lead to a straightforward win\n\nAnswer: R: a1-a2"}
