al pressure.\n\nReason: R: e3-e2 is the most forcing move. It gives check, pushing the White King further from the center and its pawns. After the King moves (likely Kc1, Kc3, Kb1, Kb3, or Kd1), my Rook controls the critical second rank, preventing the White King from becoming active. This move maintains maximum pressure and restricts White's options while I can then advance my King and pawns to convert my material advantage methodically.\n\nAnswer: R: e3-e2"}
