\nReason: In King + Queen + Bishop vs King endgames, the winning technique is to systematically restrict the enemy king to smaller areas, then deliver checkmate. **Q: h6-h5+** is the most forcing move - it gives check and begins driving the White king toward the edge of the board where it can be mated. After the king moves, I can continue coordinating my pieces to create a mating net. Checks are generally preferred in these endgames as they force the opponent's hand and accelerate the mate.\n\nAnswer: Q: h6-h5"}
